-- examples/checks/agg-unknown-beside-hole.rofl — `unknown(A)` BESIDE A HOLE
-- IS A SHRUG, in both engines, under either evaluator (docs/aggregates.md,
-- "Shrugs, as built"): it was refused (f_unknown_is_read_as_complete_beside_a_hole,
-- f_unknown_beside_a_hole_was_guarded_only_under_well_founded), and now what a
-- hole left out, A, makes `unknown(A)` no answer, read positively or under
-- not, while what is known is decided. Four programs: an overflow
-- (holes-negation-unknown.rofl), a type error (-type), a positive reader
-- (-positive), and a hole that keeps a fact from being staged
-- (holes-negation-ticks-unknown.rofl). Two ticks: each tick's shrugs, read as
-- data, are carried to the one the state is read at, and so are the answers.
aub_shrug(A)@next :- shrug(A, inherited, _).
aub_shrug(A)@next :- aub_shrug(A).
aub_held(hu, A)@next :- hu_decided(A).
aub_held(hut, A)@next :- hut_decided(A).
aub_held(P, A)@next :- aub_held(P, A).
-- expect-row: aub_shrug[main](hu_decided(c))
-- expect-row: aub_shrug[main](hut_decided(c))
-- expect-row: aub_shrug[main](hup_maybe(c))
-- expect-row: aub_shrug[main](hk_decided(c))
-- expect-row: aub_held[main](hu,k)
-- expect-row: aub_held[main](hut,k)
-- expect-no-row: aub_held[main](hu,c)
-- expect-no-row: aub_held[main](hut,c)
-- expect-no-row: aub_shrug[main](hu_decided(k))
-- expect-no-row: aub_shrug[main](hk_decided(k))
